From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:23:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: check the targeting range before computing the
 visibility

TargetingConditions#test computed LivingEntity#getVisibilityPercent (a loop
over all equipment slots with component lookups) for every candidate target
before comparing the distance. The visibility is clamped to 10, so a target that
is out of range even at the maximum visibility is now rejected first. The
targeting goals (NearestAttackableTargetGoal, ...) test every nearby entity.

Behaviour: identical results.

Ported from Leaf/Gale "Check targeting range before getting visibility" by Martijn Muijsers
<martijnmuijsers@live.nl>, based on Airplane "Early return optimization for target
finding" by Paul Sauve <paul@technove.co> (GPL-3.0-only, Copyright (C) 2020 Technove LLC).
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/targeting/TargetingConditions.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/targeting/TargetingConditions.java
index bd6d9fdeb468428bdf35e888be141293088228a4..28c7f12039931b621983594cfb53f9e7d979f2db 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/targeting/TargetingConditions.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/targeting/TargetingConditions.java
@@ -79,9 +79,18 @@ public class TargetingConditions {
             }
 
             if (this.range > 0.0) {
+                double distanceToSqr = targeter.distanceToSqr(target.getX(), target.getY(), target.getZ());
+                // Leaf port start - reject targets that are out of range even at the maximum visibility (LivingEntity#getVisibilityPercent is clamped to
+                // MobVisibility.MAX_VISIBILITY) before computing the visibility, which loops over all equipment slots (Leaf/Gale "Check targeting range before
+                // getting visibility", based on Airplane "Early return optimization for target finding" by Paul Sauve; GPL-3.0-only)
+                double maxVisibilityDistance = Math.max(this.range * (this.testInvisible ? net.minecraft.world.item.component.MobVisibility.MAX_VISIBILITY : 1.0), 2.0);
+                if (distanceToSqr > maxVisibilityDistance * maxVisibilityDistance) {
+                    return false;
+                }
+                // Leaf port end
+
                 double modifier = this.testInvisible ? target.getVisibilityPercent(level, targeter) : 1.0;
                 double visibilityDistance = Math.max(this.range * modifier, 2.0);
-                double distanceToSqr = targeter.distanceToSqr(target.getX(), target.getY(), target.getZ());
                 if (distanceToSqr > visibilityDistance * visibilityDistance) {
                     return false;
                 }
